  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &219809191
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 219809190}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 15b66a59bd566a54caaf2e3143e367d7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - 'Despair: Welcome Traveler, I believe you met my brother rage, I am despair.'
  - 'Traveller: I believe you have a story of your own like your brother?'
  - 'Despair: Indeed, each one of us has his own story. Mine was opposite of my brother,
    I had it all, the money the family the friends. I lived a happy life and I was
    content with everything...'
  - 'Despair: Till one day I met a girl, she wasn''t from my village she was from
    outside, and I fell in love with her...'
  - "Despair: My family warned me about her. They said something in their intuition
    felt wrong, her energy was unsettling, and being around her didn\u2019t feel
    safe."
  - 'Despair: Like any man blinded by love, I ignored their warnings. When your heart
    is consumed, common sense fades, and the signs that anyone else would notice
    slip quietly out of sight.'
  - 'Despair: Then one day, the girl I loved asked me to leave with her to meet her
    parents and see the village she called home.'
  - 'Despair: At first I was hesitant but I collected the courage and I told my family
    I am going to travel with her...'
  - "Despair: At first, they didn\u2019t like the idea, but eventually they gave
    in. At dawn we set out, passing through mountains, lakes, and countless places
    along the way.."
  - 'Despair: At last, we arrived at a village that seemed half in ruins. We stepped
    inside, and the moment I crossed the threshold of the house, a sudden blow struck
    the back of my head.'
  - 'Despair: I awoke shackled to a heavy iron ball. The girl sat before me on a
    chair, her family gathered around her. My head throbbed with pain, and as I struggled
    against the pounding ache, she finally spoke...'
  - "Despair: She looked me in the eye and said, \u2018You are a prisoner now. From
    this day forward, you live and work for us'. I could barely breathe as I asked,
    and what of everything we shared? What of our love?"
  - "Despair: In all coldness, she told me it had all been a lie. Her family sent
    her to lure men, to drag them back and bind them into servitude. I spat out my
    defiance \u2018My family will find me, and they will burn your village to the
    ground.\u2019 But she only stared, unshaken, for her village lay hidden, veiled
    from the world, beyond the reach of vengeance."
  - "Despair: The years dragged on, each one carving away at me as the weight of
    endless labor consumed my body. Day by day, hope slipped further from my grasp,
    until at last I collapsed worked to death. And from that death, I was reborn\u2026
    as Despair itself."
  - "Traveler: Well, Mr. Despair\u2026 I refuse to die here. Because I will find
    my answer no matter what it takes!"
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1888695316}
